WEBVTT

00:15.810 --> 00:18.450
Leo, the situation is rather unfavorable.

00:18.940 --> 00:21.180
They're coming at us in endless waves.

00:24.980 --> 00:26.630
How long will we keep this up?

00:27.080 --> 00:29.340
Isn't there something we can do?

00:33.880 --> 00:36.010
<i>I'm also concerned about Chris's movements.</i>

00:36.010 --> 00:37.650
<i>Can we take the initiative?</i>

00:37.650 --> 00:38.970
In that case, let's—

00:38.970 --> 00:41.170
<i>I will not brook action
without my permission.</i>

00:41.170 --> 00:41.990
Dad?

00:42.460 --> 00:45.240
<i>Until we have safely
 extracted the royal family,</i>

00:45.240 --> 00:49.300
<i>do not let anyone approach
 the VIP room behind you.</i>

00:49.300 --> 00:50.170
But—

00:50.780 --> 00:52.450
<i>Leo, what should we do?</i>

00:52.450 --> 00:54.020
President's orders.

00:54.020 --> 00:56.400
We stay put and focus
 on defending this place.

00:56.400 --> 00:57.990
<i>Then what happens to Chris?</i>

01:01.830 --> 01:03.750
Concentrate on the mission at hand!

01:19.190 --> 01:21.830
I am so blind

01:21.830 --> 01:23.830
Still running

01:24.110 --> 01:27.050
Running out of sight

01:27.050 --> 01:28.700
In the night

01:28.700 --> 01:31.210
I'm feeling goosebumps

01:32.580 --> 01:39.680
Betting against the odds again,
I'm being swayed like in a dance

01:39.680 --> 01:44.350
No more Blah Blah Bluff-filled Table

01:45.960 --> 01:47.840
Just tell me how to figure it out

01:47.840 --> 01:49.650
Inside my head, I'm painting the town

01:49.650 --> 01:50.860
Addition is affliction

01:50.860 --> 01:51.730
Something's missing

01:51.730 --> 01:53.550
(Oh you really got me wrong)

01:53.550 --> 01:55.410
I wanna get out so I'm taking a chance

01:55.410 --> 01:56.270
I gotta advance

01:56.270 --> 01:57.460
You know who I am?

01:57.460 --> 01:58.910
I'm a trickster

01:59.780 --> 02:01.370
Just take a chance

02:01.370 --> 02:02.540
Play the game

02:02.540 --> 02:04.540
It sounds insane

02:04.540 --> 02:07.710
Fate smiles at the borderline

02:07.710 --> 02:14.050
Rather than dance to someone else's tune,
I wanna dance to my own.

02:14.050 --> 02:16.010
Yea I'm moving like that

02:16.010 --> 02:17.310
Give it a try

02:17.310 --> 02:18.430
Keep on going down

02:18.430 --> 02:21.110
I just need something real

02:21.110 --> 02:24.680
Then we need no fakes

02:24.680 --> 02:28.940
I'll let my soul be wild and free

02:43.720 --> 02:45.510
Why did you shoot Chris?!

02:45.740 --> 02:48.090
It was Master Theodore's orders.

02:48.090 --> 02:50.770
I will use any means necessary to stop him.

02:50.990 --> 02:52.770
Even if that means killing him?

02:53.300 --> 02:55.400
X-Hand is prohibited.

02:55.750 --> 02:59.520
I know that! I won't let him
 play a four of a kind.

02:59.520 --> 03:02.530
You are no longer a part of Pinochle.

03:02.530 --> 03:03.960
What could you possibly do?

03:04.290 --> 03:06.160
I'm fired, aren't I?

03:06.160 --> 03:08.160
So I don't have to follow your rules.

03:08.160 --> 03:11.000
We'd like to ask that you stay in line.

03:12.860 --> 03:14.250
What do you want?

03:14.250 --> 03:14.920
Out of my way—

03:18.440 --> 03:22.720
If you insist on interrupting our mission,
we'll simply have to remove you.

03:23.050 --> 03:26.150
Chris...

03:29.500 --> 03:34.230
Just like I promised, Michel,
let's continue our date from the other day.

03:36.310 --> 03:39.490
Your big brother will get 
you there... no matter what.

03:47.990 --> 03:49.710
This is where Chris went?

03:52.200 --> 03:54.000
Finn Oldman?!

03:56.810 --> 03:58.630
You stay in the car.

03:59.350 --> 04:00.510
Come on!

04:00.910 --> 04:02.300
You two right there!

04:03.380 --> 04:05.060
I need to question that man.

04:05.060 --> 04:06.510
Unhand him at once.

04:07.940 --> 04:08.940
Don't.

04:09.250 --> 04:11.150
This is Pinochle business.

04:11.150 --> 04:14.110
We don't need your assistance, missy.

04:14.900 --> 04:17.060
Pinochle this, Pinochle that!

04:17.060 --> 04:19.780
I don't know what it's all about, but...

04:19.780 --> 04:21.280
Don't underestimate the police!

04:25.150 --> 04:27.700
Whoa, hey! Are you okay?

04:28.210 --> 04:29.290
Nice timing.

04:29.290 --> 04:30.490
Come again?

04:30.830 --> 04:33.040
Nice timing!

04:34.830 --> 04:35.750
Hey!

04:35.980 --> 04:38.250
Hold it, you bastard!

04:38.710 --> 04:41.180
I'm borrowing your car, Ms. Detective!

04:41.760 --> 04:45.010
Hope you don't mind!
Call it an extralegal measure!

04:48.050 --> 04:49.560
Hey, what's going on?!

04:49.560 --> 04:50.750
Chelsea?!

04:50.750 --> 04:51.730
Why are you here?!

04:53.310 --> 04:55.750
Oh, whatever. Try not to bite your tongue!

05:02.130 --> 05:06.080
Let's call this an extralegal measure too.

05:06.080 --> 05:08.850
H-Hey, I thought you were with the police!

05:08.850 --> 05:10.870
She stole my car!

05:15.330 --> 05:16.790
And where is she?

05:16.790 --> 05:20.090
My darling girlfriend is in the car.

05:22.370 --> 05:23.840
Oh, hey!

05:24.360 --> 05:27.680
She's sleeping so peacefully. 
Could you give her a break?

05:27.680 --> 05:31.700
You know how it is, right, sweetheart?

05:31.700 --> 05:32.530
Go.

05:33.010 --> 05:35.000
Thanks so much!

05:35.990 --> 05:36.860
Hold on.

05:38.690 --> 05:42.360
Your biker jacket matches what was reported.

05:42.780 --> 05:44.520
I'll need to search you.

05:44.520 --> 05:45.980
Hands on the hood of the car.

06:05.510 --> 06:09.600
Betraying Pinochle, outwitting the Klondikes,

06:09.600 --> 06:14.520
and trying to unleash the power 
of the cards for your own purposes?

06:15.070 --> 06:16.770
I like your style.

06:17.130 --> 06:19.550
Ban Klondike.

06:20.190 --> 06:23.530
The power we players wield is special.

06:23.530 --> 06:26.530
It shouldn't be controlled, 
but used as we see fit.

06:27.210 --> 06:30.280
I don't care about the country or the crown.

06:30.790 --> 06:33.280
Do what feels right for you.

06:34.020 --> 06:35.790
Follow your heart.

06:43.420 --> 06:45.230
Ban Klondike...

06:45.640 --> 06:47.070
What is he thinking?

06:48.250 --> 06:50.700
No, it doesn't matter.

06:51.020 --> 06:54.810
As long as I can save Michel, I don't care.

06:57.660 --> 07:00.310
What? He's going to sacrifice himself?

07:00.310 --> 07:01.560
No way...

07:02.020 --> 07:08.030
Chris's dad did the same thing when 
he played a four of a kind to save Chris.

07:08.420 --> 07:13.820
So he probably intends to trade
 his own life to save Michel.

07:16.340 --> 07:17.330
That idiot.

07:19.340 --> 07:21.540
Given the direction he drove off in,

07:21.540 --> 07:24.590
I'm pretty sure he's headed
 for central Shield.

07:24.860 --> 07:27.010
Hey, you saw Chris, didn't you?

07:27.490 --> 07:29.670
Did he say anything?

07:29.670 --> 07:31.010
Like where he's going?

07:31.980 --> 07:32.840
Anything?

07:34.850 --> 07:40.010
He was his usual self, going on about 
how he had a date to keep and stuff.

07:40.010 --> 07:42.740
A date at a time like this?

07:44.260 --> 07:45.230
Hold on.

07:45.790 --> 07:48.000
Chris is with Michel, right?

07:48.000 --> 07:49.150
So this "date"...

07:50.220 --> 07:53.510
Before we go, I want to ride 
the Ferris wheel in Pott Park.

07:54.050 --> 07:57.240
Remember that time the three of 
us did it when we were little?

07:57.980 --> 08:01.500
The city looked so pretty from the top...

08:02.140 --> 08:03.400
I remember.

08:03.950 --> 08:05.880
But we'll save that for next time.

08:06.250 --> 08:07.400
You have my word.

08:07.400 --> 08:08.250
But...

08:10.490 --> 08:11.680
The Ferris wheel!

08:11.680 --> 08:12.460
Gotta be!

08:12.460 --> 08:15.010
He's that kind of stupid romantic!

08:17.000 --> 08:20.020
<i>I see... Pott Park, you say?</i>

08:20.020 --> 08:21.770
<i>That's a possibility.</i>

08:21.770 --> 08:24.990
<i>The police radio indicated earlier than an SUV</i>

08:24.990 --> 08:28.520
<i>broke through a checkpoint en route to Firth.</i>

08:28.520 --> 08:29.760
Old man?!

08:29.760 --> 08:30.630
<i>Eyes forward.</i>

08:30.630 --> 08:32.780
<i>Safe driving comes first.</i>

08:32.780 --> 08:35.690
<i>I've been listening in for a while.</i>

08:35.690 --> 08:38.530
<i>It was exciting, like playing spy.</i>

08:42.920 --> 08:45.540
Oh, good. You're awake.

08:46.730 --> 08:48.040
<i>Finn.</i>

08:48.590 --> 08:53.480
We've been ordered to track down Chris 
with every resource at Pinochle's disposal.

08:53.480 --> 08:57.430
Are you trying to get in our way?

08:57.650 --> 08:58.520
Yeah.

08:58.520 --> 09:02.990
<i>We're collecting cards 
at the behest of the king.</i>

09:02.990 --> 09:06.440
<i>Standing against Pinochle means 
standing against the country.</i>

09:06.440 --> 09:10.430
<i>Do you mean to stick 
to your guns even if it means</i>

09:10.430 --> 09:13.940
<i>making an enemy of His Majesty? Of Fourland?</i>

09:14.180 --> 09:14.870
<i>Yeah.</i>

09:14.870 --> 09:17.650
<i>Whether it's the country 
or the crown, so be it.</i>

09:17.650 --> 09:22.450
Chris is risking his life to save Michel.

09:22.920 --> 09:26.340
To stop him, even knowing that...

09:26.780 --> 09:31.710
Finn, are you truly prepared to do this?

09:37.410 --> 09:40.300
<i>I'm his buddy.</i>

09:41.550 --> 09:45.930
When I was on my own, he stood by me.

09:46.290 --> 09:51.630
He said we were only colleagues, 
but he made sure I wasn't alone.

09:51.940 --> 09:56.290
It's my turn to stick by his side.

09:56.860 --> 09:57.990
Finn...

09:58.450 --> 10:00.450
I won't let him die if it kills me.

10:00.970 --> 10:02.950
He's my buddy!

10:04.610 --> 10:07.710
You've become great buddies indeed.

10:25.310 --> 10:27.810
You're the woman from that night...

10:27.810 --> 10:33.320
Unfortunately, I can't let you 
get to the 5 of hearts, boy.

10:39.820 --> 10:40.860
Chelsea?!

10:40.860 --> 10:42.570
Try not to bite your tongue!

10:44.350 --> 10:45.470
Who do we have here?

10:50.190 --> 10:52.330
Who's the girl?

10:54.490 --> 10:55.370
Hey...

10:58.010 --> 10:59.820
Chelsea, are you all right?

10:59.820 --> 11:01.590
Couldn't be better!

11:02.750 --> 11:04.760
Hurry and find Chris.

11:04.760 --> 11:05.850
B-But...

11:06.090 --> 11:08.600
It's fine! Just go!

11:09.030 --> 11:12.100
Go take care of that big dummy.

11:21.030 --> 11:23.030
What? Finn's on it?

11:23.470 --> 11:26.790
Yes, he is on his way to Chris.

11:26.790 --> 11:28.960
I see! If that's the case...

11:29.290 --> 11:33.790
Dad, after we clear the enemies besieging
 the VIP room and things settle down,

11:33.790 --> 11:35.540
we'll join Finn's search for Chris!

11:35.800 --> 11:37.500
<i>There's no need for that.</i>

11:37.500 --> 11:38.550
Dad, I—

11:38.770 --> 11:39.920
I told you.

11:40.370 --> 11:45.290
<i>You're too close to Chris Redgrave.
Your judgment is compromised.</i>

11:45.290 --> 11:46.300
But I—

11:46.640 --> 11:48.490
<i>What can you do?</i>

11:48.490 --> 11:50.490
<i>Just leave it to Owen.</i>

11:51.130 --> 11:51.940
I...

11:55.810 --> 12:00.140
<i>Leo, you just need to do what you were told.</i>

12:15.530 --> 12:18.210
I am Leo Constantine Pinochle...

12:19.180 --> 12:21.550
the leader of High Card!

12:37.140 --> 12:38.610
So, Dad—

12:41.000 --> 12:42.910
Dad?

12:43.350 --> 12:44.910
<i>You bought enough time.</i>

12:44.910 --> 12:46.360
<i>The mission was a success.</i>

12:46.600 --> 12:49.890
Remain on standby for further orders.

12:57.060 --> 13:00.700
Vijay, Wendy, we've neutralized 
the opposition inside the palace.

13:01.180 --> 13:03.140
We'll now pursue Chris and Finn.

13:03.820 --> 13:06.050
High Card, mobilize.

13:12.170 --> 13:14.280
Shall we, Michel?

13:22.040 --> 13:24.390
Damn it! Why are the Klondikes...

13:33.950 --> 13:38.410
I thought I warned you not 
to interfere with the family.

13:38.410 --> 13:39.960
I just want Chris to—

13:40.210 --> 13:43.240
That's interfering, boy.

13:43.240 --> 13:45.720
If you hold it against someone,
hold it against Ban.

13:55.770 --> 13:58.030
It's been ages since it was Love-P time!

13:58.030 --> 13:59.970
I love, love, love you all!

13:59.970 --> 14:03.570
In fact, I love you so much,
I'll love you <i>to death</i>!

14:03.850 --> 14:05.810
You're the samurai girl from Pinochle.

14:06.320 --> 14:09.730
Oh! I'm just so scared, I might wet myself!

14:09.730 --> 14:13.350
I gotta hurry to the ladies' room,
so I'll fillet you in a flash!

14:17.460 --> 14:18.800
Old man?!

14:18.800 --> 14:20.710
Come! Now's your chance!

14:22.110 --> 14:25.650
Aw, the boy with the face 
of a petty criminal is leaving!

14:25.650 --> 14:28.720
I wanted to slice open his thighs!

14:29.660 --> 14:34.220
Who knew helping the 5 of hearts achieve 
his dream would be such a pain?

14:34.620 --> 14:36.730
Ban's a bit <i>too</i> obsessed.

14:36.990 --> 14:38.060
What's this?

14:38.060 --> 14:41.980
What tricks are you up to, you old broad?

14:42.260 --> 14:44.230
You're in my way!

14:44.450 --> 14:46.070
You geisha *****!

14:46.740 --> 14:51.740
Oh no, you shouldn't say 
stuff like that, you ****!

15:11.760 --> 15:13.810
What the heck is going on?!

15:13.810 --> 15:16.770
I can't keep up...

15:18.840 --> 15:20.580
Hello. It's been a while.

15:20.580 --> 15:22.590
You're the Klondike from that night!

15:23.640 --> 15:26.170
Kill, kill, kill, kill, kill, kill, kill!

15:39.480 --> 15:41.460
Ah, this feels so good!

15:41.460 --> 15:43.000
More, please!

15:43.410 --> 15:45.630
Stop destroying the city!

15:45.630 --> 15:48.380
Say, why don't you give up?

15:48.380 --> 15:50.290
You see this gun I'm holding, don't you?

15:50.290 --> 15:52.550
Do as I say, or else—

15:54.010 --> 15:57.040
Or else... I-I'll shoot...

15:57.040 --> 15:58.030
Rookie.

15:58.360 --> 16:01.270
We don't carry these for looks.

16:01.270 --> 16:02.730
Don't hesitate.

16:05.520 --> 16:07.520
You're wide open!

16:16.490 --> 16:17.820
I cut her, I cut her!

16:17.820 --> 16:19.700
It's the bloody flood!

16:20.010 --> 16:22.690
Ah, I need lots, lots more
 to sink my blade into!

16:22.690 --> 16:25.590
I don't care who! Give me more meat! 
I want meat, meat, meat!

16:27.780 --> 16:30.380
Captain! You're not too shabby.

16:30.870 --> 16:31.670
Right?

16:42.490 --> 16:43.180
Listen.

16:43.880 --> 16:50.690
When you wake up, the first thing 
you'll see will be me lying there.

16:52.110 --> 16:55.650
I know I'm really doing this for myself.

16:56.410 --> 17:00.700
I just wanted it to be 
at the most beautiful place in town.

17:01.980 --> 17:03.710
That's all.

17:06.440 --> 17:10.650
I know I'm doing the same cruel 
thing our father did for me.

17:11.450 --> 17:15.470
But even so, Michel, 
I still want you to live.

17:16.850 --> 17:19.970
I'm sorry for being a terrible older brother.

17:24.130 --> 17:24.870
Play.

17:25.500 --> 17:26.620
X-Hand.

17:33.380 --> 17:35.580
Looks like he's using his X-Hand.

17:35.580 --> 17:37.330
Isn't there a shortcut?!

17:37.330 --> 17:38.620
Unfortunately, no.

17:38.620 --> 17:41.630
Shit! Isn't there something more we can do?

17:42.690 --> 17:43.480
Finn!

17:43.480 --> 17:44.870
What's going on with Chris?!

17:44.870 --> 17:46.500
Leo! And Vijay!

17:46.810 --> 17:49.000
He's at the Ferris wheel in Pott Park!

17:49.470 --> 17:51.490
So that light was Chris's doing?!

17:51.980 --> 17:53.250
I'm begging you, Leo.

17:53.250 --> 17:55.010
Take me to Chris!

17:55.610 --> 17:56.910
It won't be cheap.

17:56.910 --> 17:58.510
Pay me back when your ship comes in.

17:59.420 --> 18:00.190
Play!

18:00.190 --> 18:01.510
"Never No Dollars"!

18:36.840 --> 18:37.830
Damn it!

18:37.830 --> 18:38.890
What's wrong, Leo?!

18:38.890 --> 18:40.720
I've exhausted my funds on hand.

18:40.940 --> 18:42.330
How humiliating.

18:44.210 --> 18:45.850
Do you remember?

18:45.850 --> 18:49.980
What a High Card needs 
is manners, grace, and...

18:50.200 --> 18:52.780
A readiness to risk your life.

18:52.780 --> 18:54.360
That's all, right?

19:01.150 --> 19:02.210
Play!

19:02.210 --> 19:04.120
"Neo New Nambu"!

19:07.970 --> 19:10.510
<i>The 2 of spades is the weakest card.</i>

19:10.870 --> 19:13.320
<i>All I can do is to shoot in a straight line.</i>

19:13.650 --> 19:15.500
<i>That's my power.</i>

19:15.990 --> 19:18.330
<i>I'm the weakest. The worst.</i>

19:18.330 --> 19:20.290
<i>So what can I do?</i>

19:21.540 --> 19:24.220
<i>I could rack my brain 
all I want and still not know.</i>

19:24.630 --> 19:27.520
<i>So I just have to be a straight shooter.</i>

19:28.360 --> 19:31.900
<i>The better the hand, the greater the toll.</i>

19:31.900 --> 19:33.270
<i>If that's the case...</i>

19:33.590 --> 19:34.470
Chris!

20:11.000 --> 20:13.690
Chris?

20:14.270 --> 20:16.930
Oh... Michel...

20:17.980 --> 20:19.720
I'm... so glad...

20:20.840 --> 20:22.060
What happened?

20:23.420 --> 20:24.740
Showdown.

20:24.740 --> 20:26.200
Three of a kind.

20:26.200 --> 20:27.750
Take that!

20:27.750 --> 20:30.420
All thanks to you, partner!

20:44.330 --> 20:46.330
Hey, you're awake.

20:46.330 --> 20:49.270
You passed out and stayed 
out cold for three days.

20:49.970 --> 20:51.520
Finn?

20:53.450 --> 20:54.520
Where's Michel?!

20:59.180 --> 21:00.780
Good morning, Chris.

21:01.390 --> 21:03.410
You sure overslept.

21:03.800 --> 21:05.020
Michel!

21:05.370 --> 21:10.160
Sorry... Could you keep it down?
 I'm in pain over here.

21:10.160 --> 21:15.480
I must say, lowering the value 
of the hand was an excellent idea.

21:15.480 --> 21:17.720
Don't give him too much credit.

21:17.720 --> 21:20.580
It may have worked out,
 but it was a risky gamble.

21:20.580 --> 21:22.550
Which I won, didn't I?

21:25.750 --> 21:26.890
Hey, Chris.

21:28.380 --> 21:30.020
I've been thinking...

21:30.330 --> 21:35.020
It doesn't have to be either-or. 
You die and Michel lives or vice versa.

21:35.390 --> 21:38.500
There's gotta be another way.

21:39.870 --> 21:42.140
A way to split your life in half to share

21:42.140 --> 21:45.100
so you can be there for each other.

21:52.270 --> 21:56.000
Following the attempted coup
 by the Klondike Family,

21:52.410 --> 21:56.700
We move on, kicking away a crisis

21:56.000 --> 21:57.770
martial law has been lifted

21:56.700 --> 22:04.120
Dare to cause a dramatic upset

21:57.770 --> 22:03.130
and Shield City is returning
 to its peaceful day to day.

22:03.130 --> 22:06.620
Still, since the attack on the palace,

22:06.140 --> 22:10.720
To those of you in the safe zone
who hate to rock the boat

22:06.620 --> 22:10.210
Ban Klondike has yet
 to make another major move.

22:10.210 --> 22:14.630
We need to remain vigilant.

22:10.720 --> 22:14.370
Over here, I'm barely surviving today

22:14.370 --> 22:16.470
In exchange for my MP

22:16.020 --> 22:20.190
Next, I have an update 
on Michel Redgrave's condition.

22:16.470 --> 22:20.330
I can't cool down this burning passion

22:20.190 --> 22:22.820
While she isn't exactly in remission,

22:20.330 --> 22:24.150
Bring it, weak-ass monsters!

22:22.820 --> 22:26.900
she's no longer in critical
 condition for the time being.

22:24.150 --> 22:27.450
With that said, my knees are shaking

22:27.450 --> 22:30.210
But I still dream on

22:27.450 --> 22:33.890
As for Chris Redgrave,
 the X-Hand took no small toll on him.

22:30.210 --> 22:34.300
Because I don't want to make myself a liar

22:34.300 --> 22:38.020
(Are you all ready?)

22:34.300 --> 22:42.440
And yet he escaped death, 
perhaps due to his power of immortality.

22:37.230 --> 22:38.850
And don't be afraid

22:38.850 --> 22:40.860
Let's get sassy

22:40.860 --> 22:44.300
I'm sharpening the senses I lost

22:42.860 --> 22:44.450
Good work.

22:44.300 --> 22:48.290
Repeating a desperate act to get in the zone

22:44.450 --> 22:49.050
Now then, how shall we 
determine Chris's punishment?

22:49.050 --> 22:53.050
We move on, welcoming any phenomenon

22:51.550 --> 22:53.050
Huh?!

22:53.050 --> 22:54.930
I'm Finn's junior?!

22:53.050 --> 22:59.610
I challenge myself on the lifeline I run on

22:54.930 --> 22:58.870
Listen, we both got fired.

22:58.870 --> 23:04.940
But while you were still in the hospital, 
I got hired again as a full-time employee.

22:59.610 --> 23:03.090
Please let it slide if I take a huge tumble

23:03.090 --> 23:08.010
I smile as I go, dedicating my whole life

23:04.940 --> 23:06.700
Leo, is this for real?

23:06.700 --> 23:07.450
It is.

23:07.450 --> 23:10.560
Hmm, that means Chris is now
 at the bottom of the hierarchy.

23:08.010 --> 23:10.730
That's why I get serious

23:10.560 --> 23:13.950
What should we ask the newbie to do?

23:10.730 --> 23:13.090
So I can leave my tracks

23:13.090 --> 23:19.100
Shake up the destiny in my hand

23:17.450 --> 23:18.580
Chris!

23:19.100 --> 23:20.890
Nice to be working with you again.

23:27.540 --> 23:31.340
Whose side... are you on?

23:35.100 --> 23:40.250
production confirmed
